      "question": "Based on the FY2024 filings, compare the primary strategic objectives of AEP and ED.",
      "expected_answer": "AEP's filing does not explicitly state a strategic objective in the provided excerpts; it lists risk factors. ED's filing states: 'Con Edison seeks to provide shareholder value through continued dividend growth, supported by earnings growth in regulated utilities and electric transmission projects.' Thus, ED has a clear shareholder-focused strategy, while AEP's excerpt concentrates on forward-looking statements and risks.",
      "predicted_answer": "**Conclusion:** The retrieved FY2024 Item 7 evidence does not contain explicitly stated primary strategic objectives for either AEP or ED; instead, it provides risk-factor disclosures that implicitly reveal strategic concerns.\n\n- **AEP FY2024:** The evidence consists entirely of forward-looking risk factors under Item 7, including: cost recovery and rate-case timing [E1][E7][E9]; building/acquiring generation and transmission (including renewables) [E1][E11]; fuel and generation reliability [E1][E10][E12]; extreme weather and operational resilience [E1][E8][E15]; and ESG/technology shifts [E3][E6]. These imply operational priorities around regulated infrastructure investment, cost recovery, and grid reliability, but no explicit \"primary strategic objective\" is stated.\n\n- **ED FY2024:** The only retrieved passage states that \"Con Edison seeks to provide shareholder value through continued dividend growth, supported by earnings growth in regulated utilities and electric transmission projects\" [E2]. It also notes risks from distributed energy resources, electrification of gas/steam, and climate policy (CLCPA/Climate Mobilization Act) [E2]. This is the closest to an explicit strategic objective in the evidence.\n\n**Sources:**\n[E1] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E2] ED_2024.html — Item 7. The Companies' Strategies May Not Be Effective To Address Changes In The External Business Environment\n[E3] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E6] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E7] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E8] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E9] AEP_